From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: enable HBR passthrough over I2S

RK3588 HDMI audio uses rockchip_i2s_tdm which transfers packed IEC61937
frames over standard I2S PCM formats (S16_LE/S24_LE/S32_LE) rather than
SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE, with IEC958_AES0_NONAUDIO set in
the HDMI codec IEC958 channel status via ALSA AES0.

Enable AUD_HBR in dw_hdmi_qp_set_audio_interface() when 8-channel
NONAUDIO is active even when fmt->bit_fmt is not IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE,
so TrueHD and DTS-HD MA passthrough use HBR mode and 768 kHz channel
status.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -396,7 +396,11 @@ static void dw_hdmi_qp_set_audio_interface(struct dw_hdmi_qp *hdmi,
 		conf0 |= I2S_BPCUV_RCV_EN;
 		break;
 	default:
-		conf0 = AUD_ASP | I2S_BPCUV_RCV_DIS;
+		conf0 = (hparms->channels == 8 &&
+			 (hparms->iec.status[0] & IEC958_AES0_NONAUDIO))
+			? AUD_HBR
+			: AUD_ASP;
+		conf0 |= I2S_BPCUV_RCV_DIS;
 		break;
 	}
 
